SECTION 2: MATHEMATICAL FRAMEWORK INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
================================================================================

PROPRIETARY NOTICE FOR THE BOTTLENECK CONSTANT (I)

The following mathematical concepts, methods, and frameworks are proprietary
intellectual property exclusively linked to ORCID 0009-0006-6874-3910:

1. THE BOTTLENECK CONSTANT (I): Defined as the resolution of the indeterminate
   form 0/0 through the cardinal operation κ ⊖ κ = I, where κ is any infinite
   cardinal. This establishes I as a functional algebraic unit rather than an
   undefined error state.

2. THE J-FIELD FRAMEWORK: The dual supersymmetric element J arising from 
   I-symmetry breaking, representing dark sector phenomena in physics.

3. CORRECTIVE TERM Ω(I): The modification to multiplication operations
   (a + bI)(c + dI) that prevents trivial collapse of the algebraic system.

4. NON-DISTRIBUTIVE ALGEBRA: The law a(b + c) = ab + ac + Δ where Δ is a
   function of the J-field, fundamentally extending traditional algebra.

5. PAIRED-PRIME SQUARE ROOT CRYPTOGRAPHY: Security systems based on numbers
   that when multiplied by pairs reveal square roots functioning as even primes.

