SECTION 3: PROHIBITION OF UNAUTHORIZED COMMERCIAL USE
================================================================================

It is EXPRESSLY PROHIBITED to implement, use, or incorporate the following
in commercial products, hardware, firmware, or AI systems without explicit
written authorization from the copyright holder:

A) FLOATING-I ARITHMETIC: Hardware or software implementation of arithmetic
   operations treating 0/0 as the functional constant I, including but not
   limited to:
   - IEEE 754-like standards for indeterminate arithmetic
   - CPU/GPU register designs for I and J values
   - Compiler optimizations treating indeterminate as non-error

B) I-FIELD PHYSICS ENGINES: Computational models using I or J for:
   - Dark matter/energy simulations
   - Singularity resolution in black holes
   - Quantum gravity calculations
   - Cosmological inflation models

C) ENTROPY ACCELERATION SYSTEMS: Propulsion or energy systems based on
   gradients of indetermination as defined in this framework.

D) INDETERMINATE MATRIX CRYPTOGRAPHY: Security implementations using the
   mathematical properties of I defined herein.

